   k=4: 1 / [1 - (1/2)^2] = 1 / (1 - 1/4) = 4/3
   k=5: 1 / [1 - (1/2)^1] = 1 / (1 - 1/2) = 2/1 = 2
4. So E = 64/63 + 32/31 + 16/15 + 8/7 + 4/3 + 2.
5. Find a common denominator and sum these fractions to get m/n in lowest terms.
6. Then compute 100m + n.
